      "playwright": "Keyboard events are Playwright's strong suit: keyboard.down/up give precise control over held keys, which is exactly what the pressed-state animation needs. Audio can't be heard in CI, so the spec checks the gate (audioState 'none' before a gesture), live voice counts and the displayed pitch instead of sound. Timing was the tricky part: an installed but running clock still counted real typing latency, so the test uses page.clock.pauseAt() plus runFor(60_000) to make WPM deterministic. Typing about 110 characters through real key events is slow under load, so that one test gets a longer timeout and reduced motion to cut paint cost.",
